        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "81f595be-f375-5179-af3a-15d17d960697",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Colocasia, Coronilla, Xanthosoma, Securigera\n- Plant Families and Genera: Araceae, Caladium, Alocasia\n- Places: southeastern Asia, the Indian subcontinent, Europe, North Africa\n- Topics: ornamental plants, horticultural names, taxonomy\n\nFacts:\n- Colocasia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Araceae that is native to southeastern Asia and the Indian subcontinent.\n- Coronilla is a genus of about 20 species of flowering plants native to Europe and North Africa.\n- Securigera is a segregate of the genus Coronilla.\n- Many species of Xanthosoma, especially Xanthosoma roseum, are used as ornamental plants.\n- In popular horticultural literature, Xanthosoma is known as ape or elephant ear because its leaf is said to resemble an elephant's ear.\n- The common name elephant ear is also sometimes applied to similar plants in the closely related genera Caladium, Colocasia, and Alocasia.",
